Context:
- User requested adding project name/root configuration and tmux/Emacs setup for Scheme development
- Implemented on FreeBSD 14.3-RELEASE with Guile3 environment

Considerations:
- Used direnv's PROJECT_NAME and PROJECT_ROOT env vars for consistency across tools
- Emacs config loads necessary packages (geiser, paredit, org, tramp) for full Scheme IDE
- Tmux session management includes TTY tracking for debugging
- Make target checks for existing sessions to prevent duplicates

Technical Decisions:
- Chose emacs -nw -Q -l for clean, terminal-based Emacs with only project config
- Configured Geiser specifically for Guile3 (FreeBSD's default Guile package)
- Added PROJECT_NAME/ROOT as Make variables with ?= for override capability
- Session name derived from PROJECT_NAME for consistency

Issues/Limitations:
- Emacs packages auto-install on first run if not present
- Requires tmux and emacs to be installed (not enforced in deps)
- TTY output from tmux list-panes helps with TRAMP or remote debugging

Timing:
- Implementation: ~5 minutes
- Testing considerations for tmux session lifecycle
- Compatible with existing mise-en-place workflow

Future Enhancements:
- Could add automatic package.el bootstrap if MELPA not configured
- Session persistence/restore capabilities
- Integration with direnv auto-hooks
